{"study_accession":"PRJNA834806","secondary_study_accession":"SRP373421","title":"LncRNA LYPLAL1-DT screening from type 2 diabetes with macrovascular complication contributes protective effects on human umbilical vein endothelial cells via regulating the miR-204-5p/SIRT1 axis.","description":"Long noncoding RNAs (lncRNAs) are involved in diabetes related diseases. However, the role of lncRNAs in the pathogenesis of type 2 diabetes with macrovascular complication (DMC) has seldomly been recognized. This study screened lncRNA profiles of leukocytes from DMC patients and explored protective role of lncRNA LYPLAL1-DT in endothelial cells (EC) under high glucose (HG) and inflammatory conditions (IS). Between DMC and healthy controls, 477 differential expression lncRNAs (DE-lncRNAs) were identified. The enrichment and pathway analysis showed that most of the DE-lncRNAs belonged to inflammatory, metabolic, and vascular diseases. A total of 12 lncRNAs was validated as significant DE-lncRNAs in expanding cohorts. Furthermore, these DE-lncRNAs were shown to be significantly related to hypoxia, HG, and IS in EC, especially lncRNA LYPLAL1-DT. LYPLAL1-DT overexpression results in the promotion of the proliferation, and migration of EC, as well as an elevation of autophagy. Overexpressed LYPLAL1-DT reduces the adhesion of monocytes to EC, boosts anti-inflammation, and suppresses inflammatory molecules secreted in the medium. Mechanistically, LYPLAL1-DT acts as competing endogenous RNA (ceRNA) by downregulating miR-204-5p, therefore enhancing SIRT1 and protecting EC autophagy function; thus, alleviating apoptosis. Finally, exosome sequencing revealed LYPLAL1-DT expression was 4 times lower in DMC cells than in healthy samples. In general, we identified LYPLAL1-DT having protective effects on EC as ceRNA mediated through the miR-204-5p/SIRT1 pathway. Therefore, it inhibits the autophagy of EC as well as modulating systemic inflammation. This approach could be regarded as a new potential therapeutic target in DMC. Overall design: gene expression profiling analysis of RNA-seq data for 6 patients diagnosed with DMC(type 2 diabetes with macrovascular complication) and 6 health controls","pubmed":"","geo_series":"","n_samples":12,"samples":[{"sample_accession":"SAMN28061047","study_accession":"PRJNA834806","blood_class":"plasma_serum_cfrna","class_from":"sample","title":"MAD6","description":"MAD6","sex":"","geo_sample":"GSM6098681","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2022-05-06","attributes":[["source_name","blood serum"],["tissue","blood serum"],["disease","diabetic macrovascular disease"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"SRR19062427","experiment_accession":"SRX15133704","library_layout":"PAIRED","library_selection":"cDNA","instrument_model":"HiSeq X Ten","read_count":39480988,"base_count":11844296400,"first_public":"2022-05-06","experiment_title":"HiSeq X Ten sequencing: GSM6098681: MAD6 Homo sapiens RNA-Seq"}],"labels":[],"single_cell":false},{"sample_accession":"SAMN28061048","study_accession":"PRJNA834806","blood_class":"plasma_serum_cfrna","class_from":"sample","title":"MAD5","description":"MAD5","sex":"","geo_sample":"GSM6098680","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2022-05-06","attributes":[["source_name","blood serum"],["tissue","blood serum"],["disease","diabetic macrovascular disease"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"SRR19062428","experiment_accession":"SRX15133703","library_layout":"PAIRED","library_selection":"cDNA","instrument_model":"HiSeq X Ten","read_count":36445405,"base_count":10933621500,"first_public":"2022-05-06","experiment_title":"HiSeq X Ten sequencing: GSM6098680: MAD5 Homo sapiens RNA-Seq"}],"labels":[],"single_cell":false},{"sample_accession":"SAMN28061049","study_accession":"PRJNA834806","blood_class":"plasma_serum_cfrna","class_from":"sample","title":"MAD4","description":"MAD4","sex":"","geo_sample":"GSM6098679","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2022-05-06","attributes":[["s